      "taxonomyCrosswalkNote": "The exact CAS IPT row records the species-rank binomial Taenioides caeculus but has no scientificNameAuthorship or identifiedBy value; the 1837 authorship is assigned in GBIF/older ITIS, not stated in the CAS row. The current Catalog of Fishes query for Taenioides caeculus returns no record, while its current entry for the original Valenciennes combination Amblyopus caeculus maps it as a synonym of Taenioides anguillaris (Linnaeus 1758). WoRMS and FishBase likewise treat the formal Bloch & Schneider 1801 Taenioides caeculus name as T. anguillaris. FishBase/CLOFFA distinguish a separate explicitly non-Schneider misapplication associated with T. cirratus; no source evidence links this CAS item to that misapplication. Use T. anguillaris only as a nomenclatural crosswalk, retain the CAS binomial and GBIF label verbatim, and do not interpret this as specimen re-identification, current presence, or a complete checklist."
